        </header>

        <section class="gh-content gh-canvas is-body">
            <blockquote>🆓 <strong>Free article</strong> · Anyone can read this article for free</blockquote><p>The game runs. The new graphics option does not.</p><p>That is when the specifications get another reading. Is the PC falling behind, or does the new feature have a separate admission ticket?</p><p><a href="https://www.vlsi.kr/en/nvidia-vera-cpu-bandwidth-en/">NVIDIA</a>'s <a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/geforce/news/nba-2k27-dlss-5-3d-guided-neural-rendering-geforce-game-ready-driver/?ref=vlsi.kr">September 3 Game Ready announcement for NBA 2K27</a> makes that distinction concrete. <strong>Running the game and enabling DLSS 5's new visual feature have different requirements.</strong></p><h2 id="the-recommended-list-says-rtx-2070-the-new-option-says-rtx-50">The recommended list says RTX 2070. The new option says RTX 50.</h2><p><a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/4356430/NBA_2K27/?ref=vlsi.kr">Steam recommends</a> an RTX 2070 with 8GB of VRAM among its GPU choices. NVIDIA's local support for DLSS 5 3D-Guided Neural Rendering covers the RTX 50 series. Meeting a game's recommended specifications does not mean every new graphics feature will be available.</p><figure class="kg-card kg-image-card kg-card-hascaption"><img src="https://storage.ghost.io/c/e0/1d/e01dab3f-8599-4f20-85b3-3b2507a10672/content/images/2026/10/dlss-flow.png" class="kg-image" alt="Flow diagram separating the roles of DLSS 5, Multi Frame Generation and Reflex" loading="lazy"><figcaption>DLSS 5 neural rendering (lighting and materials), Multi Frame Generation (displayed frames) and Reflex (latency) do three different jobs. Per the article.</figcaption></figure><p>An existing PC therefore raises two questions: can it deliver an enjoyable game, and is the new lighting and material treatment worth an additional expense? <em>Recommended specifications are not a promise of a particular frame rate at your chosen resolution.</em></p><h2 id="better-looking-frames-and-additional-frames-do-different-jobs">Better-looking frames and additional frames do different jobs</h2><p>In <a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/geforce/news/dlss-5-3d-guided-neural-rendering/?ref=vlsi.kr">NVIDIA's technical explanation</a>, the neural-rendering stage enriches lighting and materials on the foundation of the engine-rendered frame. It uses a one-frame-in, one-frame-out model. Multi Frame Generation produces additional frames. Features that work together need not do the same job.</p><figure class="kg-card kg-image-card kg-card-hascaption"><img src="https://storage.ghost.io/c/e0/1d/e01dab3f-8599-4f20-85b3-3b2507a10672/content/images/2026/10/concept-dlss.jpg" class="kg-image" alt="Concept image of neural rendering on a transparent-shroud graphics card with a basketball game scene" loading="lazy"><figcaption>A GPU whose neural rendering enriches lighting and materials in a basketball game scene — image quality and frame generation must be judged separately.</figcaption></figure><p>NVIDIA's figure of <strong>up to 370 FPS on an RTX 5090 at 4K, Ultra settings and ray tracing</strong> combines multiple DLSS features, including Super Resolution and Multi Frame Generation. It is a vendor result, not a measurement of the neural-rendering feature in isolation.</p><p>Image quality and responsiveness also deserve separate checks. A displayed frame rate that includes generated frames cannot, by itself, tell you the delay between pressing a button and seeing a response. <a href="https://docs.nvidia.com/datacenter/tesla/driver-installation-guide/gaming.html?ref=vlsi.kr">NVIDIA distinguishes Frame Generation from its latency-reducing Reflex technology.</a> For a useful comparison, hold resolution and other settings constant, then inspect the image, frame pacing and controls with neural rendering toggled.</p><figure class="kg-card kg-image-card kg-card-hascaption"><img src="https://storage.ghost.io/c/e0/1d/e01dab3f-8599-4f20-85b3-3b2507a10672/content/images/2026/09/dlss-three-roles.png" class="kg-image" alt="DLSS 5 addresses image appearance, Multi Frame Generation displayed frame count, and Reflex PC latency. Evaluate the effects separately." loading="lazy"><figcaption>VLSI Korea original schematic. DLSS 5 addresses image appearance, Multi Frame Generation displayed frame count, and Reflex PC latency. Evaluate the effects separately. Sources: <a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/geforce/news/dlss-5-3d-guided-neural-rendering/?ref=vlsi.kr">www.nvidia.com</a>, <a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/geforce/technologies/reflex/?ref=vlsi.kr">www.nvidia.com</a>.</figcaption></figure><h2 id="the-buying-decision-starts-with-the-equipment-you-already-own">The buying decision starts with the equipment you already own</h2><p>The <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/4356430/NBA_2K27/?cc=us&ref=vlsi.kr">U.S. Steam base-game listing</a> checked on September 5 is $69.99. That is not a converted Korean price or a verified tax-inclusive checkout total. It cannot stand in for the cost of replacing a GPU as well as buying the game.</p><p>For someone who already owns both an RTX 50 PC and the game, trying the setting comes first. An older-GPU owner faces a larger question: does this change in one game's presentation justify replacing hardware? Developers also have to consider the supported audience and the combinations they must test. That is an operational implication of the compatibility boundary, not a sales forecast.</p><p>Cloud gaming offers another route, with qualifications. <a href="https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/geforce-now-thursday-september-2026-games-list/?ref=vlsi.kr">NVIDIA specifies</a> Ultimate members using RTX 5080-powered rigs in NVIDIA-operated regions. That announcement does not establish availability or prices for a Korean alliance-partner service. A fair cost comparison needs the relevant region's actual support, subscription price and connection conditions.</p><blockquote>VLSI Korea view: A PC that plays the game and a PC that enables every new graphics option answer different buying questions.</blockquote><h2 id="product-economics-specifications">Product economics &amp; specifications</h2>
<!--kg-card-begin: html-->
<table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Details</th><th>Buyer implication</th><th>Evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Base game (U.S.)</th><td>NBA 2K27 Standard/base game: USD 69.99, Steam U.S., checked Sep 5, 2026; no discount. Final tax treatment not verified.</td><td>Game-only price; excludes GPU, PC and optional purchases. Not a Korean quote.</td><td>verified · <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/api/appdetails?appids=4356430&cc=us&l=english&ref=vlsi.kr">Source</a></td></tr><tr><th>DLSS feature / hardware cost</th><td>No standalone DLSS 5 price is listed in the launch materials; regional GPU and cloud subscription quotes were not verified.</td><td>Do not compare a full GPU replacement with the game price alone.</td><td>unavailable · unavailable</td></tr><tr><th>Likely first users</th><td>Players who already own both an RTX 50 PC and NBA 2K27.</td><td>Try the visual option before treating it as a hardware-buying reason. Buyer-fit analysis, not verified adoption.</td><td>analysis · analysis</td></tr><tr><th>Local feature support</th><td>RTX 50 series; Game Ready 616.64 WHQL; enable DLSS Neural Rendering in game.</td><td>Feature eligibility differs from the base game requirements.</td><td>verified · <a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/geforce/news/dlss-5-3d-guided-neural-rendering/?ref=vlsi.kr">Source</a></td></tr><tr><th>Base-game recommendation</th><td>One recommended GPU: RTX 2070 8GB; recommended RAM: 16GB; storage: 110GB, SSD required.</td><td>These do not guarantee DLSS 5 neural-rendering access or a target FPS.</td><td>verified · <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/api/appdetails?appids=4356430&cc=us&l=english&ref=vlsi.kr">Source</a></td></tr><tr><th>Cloud availability</th><td>GeForce NOW Ultimate, RTX 5080-powered rigs, NVIDIA-operated regions.</td><td>Check local service availability and connection conditions; do not assume Korean partner support.</td><td>verified · <a href="https://blogs.nvidia.com/blog/geforce-now-thursday-september-2026-games-list/?ref=vlsi.kr">Source</a></td></tr><tr><th>Benchmark interpretation</th><td>Vendor claim: up to 370 FPS, RTX 5090, 4K Ultra + ray tracing, multiple DLSS features enabled.</td><td>Not an isolated neural-rendering speedup or an input-latency measurement.</td><td>verified · <a href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/geforce/news/nba-2k27-dlss-5-3d-guided-neural-rendering-geforce-game-ready-driver/?ref=vlsi.kr">Source</a></td></tr></tbody></table>
<!--kg-card-end: html-->
<h2 id="share-price-context">Share-price context</h2><p><em>Share-price chart unavailable: NVIDIA IR: verified daily history unavailable.</em></p><h2 id="watch-the-official-demonstration">Watch the official demonstration</h2><p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LHUzFnq70b8&ref=vlsi.kr">NBA 2K27 | NVIDIA DLSS 5 Launch Trailer</a> · NVIDIA GeForce</p><p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=58FagrSqC4M&ref=vlsi.kr">DLSS 5 | Introducing 3D-Guided Neural Rendering</a> · NVIDIA GeForce</p><p><a href="https://investor.nvidia.com/stock-info/stock-quote-and-chart/?ref=vlsi.kr">NVIDIA's official stock page</a> provides market context. This run did not obtain a verifiable daily history; no price move is attributed to the game-feature announcement.</p><p><em>AI assisted research and writing from public original sources, with a separate independent review. Information checked September 5, 2026.</em></p><p>Disclosure</p><p><em>This article is provided for informational purposes only and does not constitute a recommendation to buy or sell any security. Figures and factual statements are based on publicly available sources, including company filings, news reports, and market research, and may contain errors in the source material or in the preparation of this article. The author may own shares in companies mentioned. All investment decisions and their outcomes are the reader's responsibility.</em></p><p><strong>Related reading</strong></p><ul><li><a href="https://www.vlsi.kr/en/daily-silicon-nvidia-96-2b-ai-silicon-and-ucie-design-shift/">Daily Silicon: NVIDIA $96.2B, AI Silicon and UCIe Design Shift</a></li><li><a href="https://www.vlsi.kr/en/daily-silicon-nvidia-81-6b-q2-guide-91b-parabolic/">Daily Silicon: NVIDIA $81.6B, Q2 Guide $91B — Parabolic</a></li><li><a href="https://www.vlsi.kr/en/daily-silicon-nvidia-d-day-triple-memory-pt-hike/">Daily Silicon: NVIDIA D-day, Triple Memory PT Hike</a></li></ul>
        </section>

